  "goodToKnow": "Der Konstrukteur (die Konstrukteurin) is a design engineer who designs machines, vehicles or structures. Famous German Konstrukteure include Ferdinand Porsche (the VW Beetle), Gottlieb Daimler and Carl Benz, and Konrad Zuse, who built the Z3, an early programmable computer, in 1941. In Formula 1, die Konstrukteurswertung is the constructors' championship. Plural: die Konstrukteure."
